rams divided by height in metres squared; &#x0003c;18.5, 18.5&#x02013;24.9, or <bold>&#x02a7e;</bold>25.0), walking duration (&#x0003c;1 or <bold>&#x02a7e;</bold>1&#x02009;h&#x02009;day<sup>&#x02212;1</sup>), family history of cancer (yes or no), smoking status (never, former, or currently), number of cigarettes smoked per day (continuous variable), years of smoking (continuous variable), alcohol drinking (never, former, currently drinking &#x0003c;45.6&#x02009;g&#x02009;day<sup>&#x02212;1</sup>, or currently drinking <bold>&#x02a7e;</bold>45.6&#x02009;g&#x02009;day<sup>&#x02212;1</sup> ethanol), total energy intake per day (continuous variable), and daily consumption of soybean products, total meat, total fish, dairy products, total fruits, and total vegetables (for each food group, continuous variable), and consumption coffee (never or occasionally, 1&#x02013;2 cups/day, or <bold>&#x02a7e;</bold>3 cups/day).</p></fn><fn id="t3-fn2"><label>a</label><p>The <italic>P</italic>-values for the test of linear trend were calculated by treating the green tea consumption category as a continuous variable.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>